{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/984143-friendly-fire-among-evil","id":984143,"title":"Friendly fire among evil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-08T18:10:38-07:00","id":984143,"title":"Friendly fire among evil","content":"The WOD has been plaqued by thousands of different evils who all have the upper hand and are only a step from victory... for about a few thousand years now. I wonder why evil just can't seem to win? Maybe it's because those evils keep killing eachother off. Here are some example's<br /> <br /> In a sidebar in werewolf it states that anything evil enough can pop up as &quot;wyrm tainted&quot; with the sense wyrm gift, but does that also work the other way around? For instance, Spectors in wraith would set off huge &quot;wyrm is here&quot; signals even though they are tainted by oblivion brand &quot;Evil&quot;. If wyrmish people popped up the same way to a spector's oblivion radar, doesn't that mean (with spector's collective efforts of killing of oblivion tainted humans to &quot;Free&quot; the oblivion in them) That they've been genociding the wyrm's primary minions for thousands of years now?<br /> <br /> Is the &quot;Abyss&quot; that the Lambrosa access with obtentration the same &quot;Abyss&quot; that the fallen occupy in DTF? With the connection they have to the abrahamic god(the curse and power of whom pretty much flow in the vampire's veins) and the fact they both are described the same(dark lightless place filled with endless darkness that removes your senses and ancient, demonic entities that dwell within), it's not hard to picture. Though you have to wonder, with how the fallen in DTF somehow know what happens to human souls in the abyss, I wonder how many desperate fell knights tried to possess an unsuspecting lambrosa only to send them both hurtling back to the abyss.<br /> <br /> Banes love to corrupt and possess people to make fomori, except vampires. Vampires can't be possessed by most banes, not without the bane drawing the short end of the stick and the vampire gaining all the benifits of possession with none of the drawbacks(except with blood or death banes). I wonder how many had to trap themselves inside immortal blood suckers before they finally figured it out.<br /> <br /> Naphndi and Earthbound have the power to summon malevolent spirits(likely wyrmish or infernal) and alien beings(f'tagn). Unfortunately said power doesn't come with the ability to Control said beings, and they usually arrive hungry.....(usually accompanied by statements of &quot;No! not Me!!!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Please share some of your own cases of evil biting it's own tail, extra points if they're funny or make an evil deity face-palm hard enough to crack skulls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T18:35:06-07:00","id":984161,"title":"","content":"A thought I've had for a while is that the Yeren, may unwittingly aid the Garou nation, by ripping pentex apart with their childish bickering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T19:13:32-07:00","id":998011,"title":"","content":"If you consider that for ghosts to exist, they require either a degree of powerful will or strong attachments to this world, but if a spirit lacks those things they automatically cease to exist/move on. This would mean that necromancers function by depleting the pool of potential spirits because the only ones they can summon are the ones who are able to maintain their existence. Thus the lands of the dead can't ever have a functional hierarchy because some necromancer decided to turn a factions leader into a cursed necklace for eternity. Haunted houses wouldn't exist because they would get raided by necromancers looking for stabilized ghosts to turn into servants or material components.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T05:16:31-08:00","id":1001718,"title":"","content":"I've generally gone with creatures that can sense alignment can, with enough suc